// EXPECT: FAIL
// ERROR_CONTAINS: ANUBIS_TAINTED_SINK_WITHOUT_DECLASSIFY
// Lead agent 2026-07-27. COMMAND INJECTION through a higher-order function, and a general false
// accept — not tied to any declared qualifier. Surfaced while chasing a narrower enum-payload probe
// from GROK-SEKHMET round 9; the control showed it leaks with an ordinary `input()` too.
//
// `apply(f, v) { f(v); }` applies its closure parameter to its OTHER parameter. The call-site
// descent bound the closure's params as FRESH UNLABELLED bindings, discarding the label of the
// argument the callee actually forwards — so untrusted input reached `shell` with nothing charged,
// while the direct `g(input())` form was correctly rejected.
//
// The fix binds those params to a conservative JOIN over the call's other arguments. Tracking which
// argument the callee forwards would need a param-to-param application summary; over-approximating
// can only over-charge a closure whose sibling argument is labelled, which is the fail-closed
// direction this file uses for every summary.
fn apply(f, v) { f(v); }
fn main() uses(shell) {
    let k = input();
    apply(|v| { shell(v); }, k);
}
